---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Animaxxing — Motion that knows when to stop" current="home">
  <article class="page shell">
    <h1>Motion that knows when to stop</h1>
    <p>
      Animaxxing is a small studio that builds interfaces for people who read them. We are
      interested in the quiet part of motion design: the moment a page arrives, the moment it
      leaves, and the half second in between where most of the damage gets done.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every screen here runs the same lifecycle. Content is laid out first and animated second, so
      nothing jumps, nothing flashes, and nothing is hidden from a reader whose script never
      loaded.
    </p>
    <p>Have a look at the work, or read about how the studio got here.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
